      "content": "9.1 Components of Microsoft Office"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Microsoft Office consists of primary productivity applications including MS Word, MS Excel, and MS PowerPoint.",
        "MS Word study focuses on core features and the structural components of the MS Word window.",
        "MS Excel covers essential spreadsheet terminology and common Excel functions.",
        "MS PowerPoint involves learning key presentation features and window components.",
        "Basic keyboard shortcuts and important exam points are vital topics frequently targeted in competitive exams."
      ],
